1) 执行 gpstate -e 查看处于非预期角色的 segment 及其所在:
1) Run gpstate -e to see which segments are in an unexpected role and which hosts they are on;
2) Check whether the host of the original primary is down or has a disk failure and fix the hardware first;
3) Run gprecoverseg to recover the failed segment and wait until gpstate -m shows everything back to Synchronized;
4) Finally run gprecoverseg -r to return the primary/mirror roles to their original distribution and confirm overall health with gpstate -s.

1) 执行 gpstate -m 确认是哪些镜像段的 Data Status 异:
1) Run gpstate -m to identify which mirror segments have an abnormal Data Status;
2) For Resynchronizing, watch the progress (gpstate -e); resynchronizing large tables legitimately takes a while, so just wait;
3) For Not Syncing, run gprecoverseg for an incremental recovery, and gprecoverseg -F for a full recovery if that fails;
4) Once recovery completes, run gprecoverseg -r to restore the original primary/mirror distribution so primaries do not stay concentrated on a few hosts.
